,"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search for `mcp/health` -> (no matches)","infra/scripts/observability.sh:298 `mcp_code=$(curl ... \"https://${DOMAIN}/mcp\" ...)` ; :299 `mcp_ok=0; [ \"$mcp_code\" = \"401\" ] && mcp_ok=1`","src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:383 `@mcp.custom_route(\"/health\", methods=[\"GET\"])`","infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template:128 `location = /mcp { proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp/mcp; }`"],"finding":"AC5 names MCP health endpoint `/mcp/health`, but no such route exists: the MCP app serves `GET /health`, and the external health probe (infra/scripts/observability.sh, nginx rebar.conf.template) is `https://<host>/mcp` expecting a 401. `/mcp/health` returns no matches anywhere in the repo.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f130b7b677db7554d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'Health evidence covers ... MCP `/mcp/health`' (and Step 5 'verify ... MCP health')","norm_id":"n882f70735ce7d6c3","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor runs the verification step and curls `/mcp/health`, gets a 404/unexpected response, and cannot produce the AC-required health evidence."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace `/mcp/health` with the real MCP serving probe: `GET https://<host>/mcp` returning 401 (per observability.sh), or the container-internal `/health` route.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attr