ty":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In step 4, state that the DSSE envelope must be signed with `sign_authorship(payload, <old-privkey-scratch-path>, principal=\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\")` so the signature keyid matches the identity the KEY_ADD verifier binds against.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'build a DSSE envelope over keyop_payload(\"KEY_ADD\", \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", <new-public-key>) via rebar.attest.authorship.sign_authorship'","src/rebar/attest/authorship.py:56 sign_authorship(payload, key_path, principal) — 'principal (the author identity's id) becomes the signature keyid (the SSHSIG principal the verifier binds against)'","src/rebar/_commands/identity.py:447 verify_authorship must verify against the identity's currently-valid keys; a keyid mismatch fails the KEY_ADD"],"finding":"Step 4's sign_authorship invocation omits the required `principal` argument, which becomes the signature keyid the KEY_ADD verifier binds against; if it is not the identity id the verify fails and the rotation is refused.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f57b1b702b2471bb2","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope and sequence, step 4 (/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key)","norm_id":"na338e04031c34123","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Envelope signed with principal set to anything other than 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d causes _verify_keyop_signature to reject the KEY_ADD, blocking the rotation after the old key has been materialized to scratch"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify the full call: `sign_authorship(keyop_payload(\"KEY_ADD\", \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", <new-public-key>), <old-priv-scratch>, principal=\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\")`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In step 4, name the serialization/argument glue: serialize the `sign_authorship(...)` Envelope with `dsse.encode` before writing the 0600 scratch file, and pass `principal=\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\"` so the KEY_ADD signature binds to the identity and decodes at `--signature-file` consume time.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'build a DSSE envelope over keyop_payload(\"KEY_ADD\", \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", <new-public-key>) via rebar.attest.authorship.sign_authorship, write the envelope to a 0600 scratch file'","`sign_authorship(payload, key_path, principal) -> dsse.Envelope` (src/rebar/attest/authorship.py:56) returns an in-memory Envelope, not serialized bytes","`_load_signature` at src/rebar/_commands/identity.py:559-571 reads the file and calls `dsse.decode(text)`, so the scratch file must be a `dsse.encode`-serialized JSON envelope","Partially-verified: the CLI surface and functions exist (MATCH), but the plan's write step underspecifies the encode/principal glue"],"finding":"Step 4 names `sign_authorship` (which returns a `dsse.Envelope` object) and `rebar identity key add --signature-file`, but omits the serialization contract between them: `--signature-file` is decoded via `dsse.decode` (expects a `dsse.encode` JSON file), and `sign_authorship` requires a `principal` argument. The plan does not name the `dsse.encode` step nor state that `principal` must be the identity id `594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f713ffffbcdf1f436","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope and sequence — step 4 (`/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key`)","norm_id":"na659ceb00ba3a344","priority":0.85,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator writes the raw Envelope repr/object to the scratch file; `rebar identity key add --signature-file` fails to decode and refuses the KEY_ADD","Operator calls sign_authorship without supplying principal=identity-id, producing an envelope whose keyid does not bind to the identity, failing verify_authorship"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State: `env = authorship.sign_authorship(keyop_payload('KEY_ADD','594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d',<new-pubkey>), key_path=<old-privkey-scratch>, principal='594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d'); write dsse.encode(env) to a 0600 scratch JSON file; then rebar identity key add 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d '<new-pubkey>' --signature-file <that-file>`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Before overwriting /auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET, capture/confirm the prior value is recoverable (e.g. record the prior SSM version or export to operator-held secure store) so the stated rollback is actually executable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b","T12"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4289,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'This invalidates active SSO sessions. Rollback requires restoring prior value from operator-held history.'","No pre-overwrite step confirms the prior value is retained/exportable."],"finding":"Step 3 (COOKIE_SIGNIN